Using Environment Variables in Jenkins Pipelines

Instead of hardcoding values into your Jenkinsfile, you can use environment variables to make your pipelines portable, secure, and easier to maintain.

How they help:
- Store values like credentials, branch names, or build IDs
- Inject variables globally (environment { }) or at stage level
- Use built-in variables like BUILD_NUMBER, JOB_NAME, and WORKSPACE
- Combine with Jenkins Credentials for secure secret handling

This keeps pipelines clean, reusable, and easier to adapt across environments.
